---
/* ============================================================
   Social — mist band, the confirmed projects beyond the railway
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   Not in the export. Added at the user's request from the borrowed
   docs/ folder — see OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #30 — which records the company
   confirming six photographed, non-railway projects as its own work
   and supplying nothing else about them. The docs are unanimous on
   how such a project may appear: a NAME, a LOCATION and a PHOTOGRAPH,
   never a case study with empty fields. That is exactly what each
   tile here carries, and why this is its own band rather than six
   more rows in Listing.astro, whose every card is built around a
   client and a figure these projects do not have.

   EVERY TILE LINKS TO ITS OWN PAGE — since 2026-09-19, when the user
   asked for one per project (OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #36; the page is
   SocialProjectPage.astro, copy in src/data/social-projects.ts). The
   link is the listing cards' own: a plain `<a class="absolute inset-0">`
   as the tile's last child, `aria-label` carrying the name, the same
   slugify() of the title. Until then a click opened the page's
   Lightbox; the photographs now open from each page's own gallery, and
   from the Gallery tab, where these projects have groups too.

   THE BAND IS MIST, between Listing (ink) and the closing CTA (ink).
   That is the surface DESIGN-SYSTEM §2's alternation asks for — and
   it closes the Listing → CTA ink-on-ink boundary that
   OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #18f recorded as built-as-drawn, without moving
   either neighbour. Kicker in the light tone, per Kicker.astro.

   THE TILES ARE GalleryGrid's tile, verbatim — the §5 media box the
   listing's small cards and every gallery tile already use: 265px,
   `object-cover`, `--kd-scrim-sm`, caption 20px in, square corners.
   Two runs of text in the caption instead of one — the small card's
   own title/meta pair (`text-d9` over `text-meta-sm`) — because a
   name and a location are two things, and the in-page editor needs a
   text leaf for each.

   FILTERS. The band carries the same two attributes the listing's
   cards do and Filters.astro treats it as one of them:
     `data-listing-view`            the Gallery tab hides it, like
                                    Listing itself.
     `data-project-status=completed` the Live tab hides it; All and
                                    Completed show it. Every photograph
                                    here is of a finished building —
                                    that is the only status they
                                    evidence, and the only one claimed.

   PENDING TILES (review only). An item with `pending` has no
   photograph. It is the same 265px box on the ink surface with a
   dashed ghost outline, the project-card badge chip carrying the
   `pending` label, the note in the body, and the same name/location
   caption — so the client sees exactly which project is missing what.
   It links to its page like the rest; the page carries the same
   placeholder where the photograph will go. `data-pending` is for
   scripts/check-placeholders.mjs. OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #32; every one is
   filled or removed before go-live.
   ============================================================ */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Kicker from "../Kicker.astro";
import { projects } from "../../data/projects";
import { galleryImage } from "../../lib/gallery-images";
import { slugify } from "../../lib/slug";

const { social } = projects;

const tiles = social.items.map((item) => ({
  item,
  image: item.file ? galleryImage(item.file) : undefined,
  href: `/projects/${slugify(item.title)}`,
}));
---

<section class="bg-kd-mist py-96" data-listing-view data-project-status="completed">
  <div class="max-w-kd mx-auto px-48">
    <Kicker label={social.kicker} editKey="projects.social.kicker" tone="light" />
    <h2 class="font-display text-d4 text-kd-ink mt-16" data-edit="projects.social.heading">
      {social.heading}
    </h2>
    <p class="text-body-sm text-kd-slate-2 mt-20 max-w-560" data-edit="projects.social.body">
      {social.body}
    </p>

    <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-16 mt-56">
      {
        tiles.map(({ item, image, href }, i) =>
          !image ? (
            <li>
              <div
                class="relative h-265 bg-kd-ink border border-dashed border-kd-ghost-outline p-20 flex flex-col"
                data-pending
              >
                <span
                  class="self-start inline-block text-badge uppercase text-kd-mist bg-kd-badge-fill border border-kd-badge-border px-8 py-6"
                  data-edit={`projects.social.items.${i}.pending`}
                >
                  {item.pending}
                </span>
                <p
                  class="text-body-sm text-kd-fog mt-16"
                  data-edit={`projects.social.items.${i}.note`}
                >
                  {item.note}
                </p>
                <div class="mt-auto">
                  <h3
                    class="font-display text-d9 text-kd-mist"
                    data-edit={`projects.social.items.${i}.title`}
                  >
                    {item.title}
                  </h3>
                  <p class="text-meta-sm text-kd-fog mt-6" data-edit={`projects.social.items.${i}.location`}>
                    {item.location}
                  </p>
                </div>
                <a href={href} class="absolute inset-0" aria-label={item.title} />
              </div>
            </li>
          ) : (
          <li>
            <figure class="relative h-265 overflow-hidden">
              <Image
                src={image}
                alt={item.alt ?? item.title}
                width={800}
                height={552}
                loading="lazy"
                class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
              />
              <div class="absolute inset-0" style="background-image: var(--kd-scrim-sm)" aria-hidden="true" />
              <figcaption class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 p-20">
                <h3 class="font-display text-d9 text-kd-mist" data-edit={`projects.social.items.${i}.title`}>
                  {item.title}
                </h3>
                <p class="text-meta-sm text-kd-fog mt-6" data-edit={`projects.social.items.${i}.location`}>
                  {item.location}
                </p>
              </figcaption>
              <a href={href} class="absolute inset-0" aria-label={item.title} />
            </figure>
          </li>
          )
        )
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
